===Etymology 2===
Sound used to form meaningless song refrains. Of imitative origin. Compare {{cog|ang|lā|pos=a common exclamation}}, {{cog|grc|λαλαγε||babble}}, {{cog|de|lallen||to babble}}.

====Interjection====
{{en-intj}}

# ''Represents the sound of music or singing''.
#: {{ux|en|"'''La la la la''', I can't hear you!" Jimmy said, sticking his fingers in his ears.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2019|author=Keira Brown|title=Between the Lines: Never in Plain Sight
|passage=The only part Lucy had to sing was the interlude, which was a bunch of '''la la la's''', and the last verse of the song, which was only four lines, and the chorus, which was just as short.}}

=====Derived terms=====
{{col|en|La-La Land
}}

===Etymology 3===
From {{der|en|enm|la}}, from {{der|en|ang|la|lā}}. More at {{m|en|lo}}.

====Alternative forms====
