# {{lb|en|often|ironic}} Prefixed to the name of a [[woman]], with [[ironic]] effect (as though an opera [[prima donna]]).
#* {{RQ:Guardian|author=Kate Carter|date=22 Nov 2007|url=https://www.theguardian.com/lifeandstyle/lostinshowbiz/2007/nov/22/graziawatch|title=Graziawatch|passage=Following lukewarm on the heels of an article a few weeks ago, where (I paraphrase due to having filed the relevant copy in the recycling bin) Victoria Beckham made a "well-meaning" remark that the other Spice Girls might want to lose a few pounds, we now have a new incidence of '''La''' Beckham's scintillating and entirely well-meaning humour.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2010|author=w:Christopher Hitchens|title=Hitch-22|publisher=Atlantic|year_published=2011|page=232
|passage=By judicious leaking, he also managed to make '''''la''''' Kirkpatrick and her associates look rather unsavory.}}
#* {{RQ:FT|edition=weekend|author=w:Jo Ellison|date=2025-06-21|title=The Bezos merger we all want a piece of|section=Life & Arts|page=22|passage=(You have to wonder where '''la''' Wintour finds the time for all this styling: maybe it's a displacement activity to fill the void left by her failure to get the Democratic party into power?)}}

