====Pronoun====
{{head|es|pronouns}}

# {{inflection of|es|ella||acc}}, [[ello#Spanish|ello]] {{q|when the antecedent's implied gender is feminine}}, and [[usted]] {{q|when referring to a woman}}; [[her]], [[it]], [[you]] (formal)
# {{n-g|impersonal neuter pronoun (accusative) in certain [[colloquial]] phrases}}: [[it]], [[this]]
#: {{ux|es|'''La''' sabe toda.|He/she knows everything ('''it''' all)}}
#: {{ux|es|¿¡Dónde '''la''' viste!?|Where did you see '''that'''!?}}
#: {{ux|es|No te '''la''' creo.|I don't believe you. (from, "I don't believe you [when it comes to] this.")}}

=====Usage notes=====
* Sometimes used where English would prefer a possessive: {{m|es||tengo algo en '''la''' bolsa|lit=I have something in the bag}} as opposed to {{m|es||tengo algo en '''mi''' bolsa|I have something in my bag}}. This is especially true with body parts and with articles of clothing or similar accessories.
* Where a feminine noun begins with '''''stressed''''' {{IPA|es|/a/}}, '''[[el]]''' is used instead: ''el alma'', ''el águila'', ''el hacha''. The article remains '''la''' where an adjective intervenes between the article and the noun: ''la majestuosa águila''. The plural remains '''las'''.

